 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 542778,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Suppose we have data that are normally distributed with mean 5 and standard deviation 1.6. Identify which data values (rounded to the nearest tenth) correspond to these percentiles: 25th (the first quartile), 80th, and 10th.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<p>3.9</p>\n<p>6.3</p>\n<p>2.9</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>When your data is normally distributed and you know the percentile, mean, and standard deviation, you can find the data value with the NORM.INV function.</p>\n<p>NORM.INV(percentile as a decimal, mean, standard deviation)</p>\n<p>For 25<sup>th</sup> percentile:</p>\n<p>In an empty cell in Google Sheets: =NORM.INV(0.25, 5, 1.6)</p>\n<p>You see: 3.9208164</p>\n<p>The approximate data value: 3.9</p>\n<p>For the 80<sup>th</sup> percentile:</p>\n<p>In an empty cell in Google Sheets: =NORM.INV(0.8, 5, 1.6)</p>\n<p>You see: 6.346593972</p>\n<p>The approximate data value: 6.3</p>\n<p>For the 10<sup>th</sup> percentile:</p>\n<p>In an empty cell in Google Sheets: =NORM.INV(0.1, 5, 1.6)</p>\n<p>You see: 2.949517497</p>\n<p>The approximate data value: 2.9</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
